      "strengths_deep_dive": [
        "Human Appeal demonstrates a high capacity for large-scale emergency response, particularly in conflict zones. In FY2023, the organization successfully scaled its revenue to <cite id=\"2\">$10.8 million</cite>, and preliminary 2024 data suggests a <cite id=\"2\">3-year revenue CAGR of 245.9%</cite>. This growth is paired with high transparency, as evidenced by their <cite id=\"1\">perfect scores of 100 in both Culture and Leadership</cite> from Charity Navigator. Their direct service model allows for immediate impact, such as the installation of <cite id=\"5\">1,027 deep water wells</cite> and the delivery of <cite id=\"6\">810 cataract surgeries</cite> to underserved populations."
      ],
      "summary": "Founded in 1991, Human Appeal Inc is a global humanitarian organization dedicated to fighting poverty and social injustice through direct aid and emergency relief. The organization has demonstrated significant growth, managing <cite id=\"2\">$10,889,699 in total revenue in FY2023</cite> and expanding its reach to support <cite id=\"4\">over 6 million beneficiaries</cite>. Their operations focus on high-urgency sectors including food security, water and sanitation, and child welfare. In Gaza alone, the charity reported providing <cite id=\"4\">4.5 million hot meals</cite> and <cite id=\"4\">59 million liters of clean water</cite> in 2024. While the organization maintains <cite id=\"1\">strong financial health with 10.7 months of working capital</cite>, it operates with a unique financial structure where the <cite id=\"1\">program expense ratio is 50.3%</cite>. This indicates that roughly half of its total spending is directed toward administrative and fundraising efforts to sustain its global infrastructure. Despite this, the charity achieves a <cite id=\"1\">high fundraising efficiency</cite>, spending only <cite id=\"1\">$0.25 to raise every $1 in donations</cite>. Human Appeal is <cite id=\"3\">fully Zakat-eligible</cite>, serving multiple categories of asnaf including the poor and needy across regions like Yemen, Syria, and Palestine.",
